SUMMARY:Operationalizing Agentic AI
DESCRIPTION:Data Science Raleigh\nAgentic AI is no longer theoretical. Sys
 tems that can reason\, plan\, and take action across workflows are enterin
 g production environments—and with them comes a new operational reality.
  The question is no longer can AI act autonomously\, but how do we stay in
  control when it does?\n\nThis webinar focuses on the practical mechanics 
 of deploying agentic AI responsibly. We’ll examine how to design governa
 nce frameworks that go beyond static guardrails\, implement observability 
 that surfaces intent and intermediate reasoning\, and maintain meaningful 
 human-in-the-loop oversight without slowing down innovation. From dynamic 
 policy enforcement to real-time monitoring and escalation paths\, we’ll 
 explore how enterprises can operationalize autonomy without sacrificing ac
 countability.\n\nIf your organization is experimenting with AI agents—or
  preparing to move from pilots to production—this session will help you 
 build systems that are not only capable\, but controllable.\n\n**What You'
 ll Learn:**\n\n1️⃣ **Governance for Autonomous Systems:** How to desig
 n policy layers\, permissioning models\, and approval workflows that align
  agent behavior with organizational risk tolerance and regulatory requirem
 ents.\n\n2️⃣ **Observability Beyond Outputs:** Why logging final respo
 nses isn’t enough—and how to instrument reasoning traces\, tool usage\
 , and memory state to create transparency in agent decision-making.\n\n3
 ️⃣ **Human-in-the-Loop by Design:** Practical patterns for escalation\
 , intervention\, and override that preserve human authority while enabling
  agents to operate efficiently across complex workflows.\n\n4️⃣ **From
  Pilot to Production Control:** The architectural considerations—modular
  workflows\, sandboxing\, audit trails\, and feedback loops—that make ag
 entic systems safe and sustainable at enterprise scale.\n\n**[Register her
 e](https://hubs.ly/Q04jJB980)**
